<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Times+New+Roman:wght@400;700&amp;family=Arial:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 0 20px;
            line-height: 1.4;
            color: #000;
            background: #fff;
        }

        h1, h2, h3 {
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            font-weight: 600;
            margin-top: 24px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }

        p {
            margin: 12px 0;
        }

        .column-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: row;
            gap: 40px;
        }

        .column {
            flex: 1;
            max-width: 48%;
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
            padding-bottom: 12px;
            margin-bottom: 24px;
        }

        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 300px;
            border: 2px dashed #999;
            background: #f5f5f5;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            margin: 20px 0;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #666;
        }

        .text-block {
            margin: 16px 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="header">
        <h1>Sample Document Title</h1>
        <p><strong>Subtitle or Document ID</strong></p>
    </div>

    <div class="column-container">
        <!-- Column 1 -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This is the first column of text.</p>
                <p>It contains multiple sentences for demonstration of layout.</p>
                <p>Text may continue here in the same column.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="placeholder">
                [Image/Chart: centered in column 1]
            </div>

            <div class="text-block">
                <p>Additional paragraph in column 1.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>List item one</li>
                    <li>List item two</li>
                    <li>List item three</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Column 2 -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This is the second column of text.</p>
                <p>Text in column 2 appears side-by-side with column 1.</p>
                <p>Relative positioning is preserved using flexbox.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="placeholder">
                [Photo/Signature: positioned in column 2]
            </div>

            <div class="text-block">
                <p>More text in column 2.</p>
                <p>Any side-by-side elements (e.g. labels next to checkboxes) would be handled with inline-block or float styling.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-block">
        <p>Single-column footer text after the two-column layout.</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```
